     - C1-A'/decomposition  at c=1 the printed decomposition counts (c-1)-1 = -1 descent steps: after step 2 the run is at W(0)=[0,0], which is TERMINAL and lies BELOW the W(1) the proof descends to. Total 2+((c-1)-1)+1 = c+1 is still correct at c=1 only because the -1 cancels the +1.
